### Euclidean Algorithm Implementation

```java
public class MathAlgorithms {
    // Iterative implementation (avoids recursion overhead)
    public static int gcd(int a, int b) {
        a = Math.abs(a);
        b = Math.abs(b);
        while (b != 0) {
            int temp = b;
            b = a % b;
            a = temp;
        }
        return a;
    }

    // LCM calculation
    public static long lcm(int a, int b) {
        if (a == 0 || b == 0) return 0;
        return ((long) Math.abs(a) / gcd(a, b)) * Math.abs(b);
    }
}
```

### Practice Problem: Sum of Arithmetic Progression

The sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic progression is given by:
$$S_n = \frac{n}{2} \cdot [2a + (n - 1)d]$$

#### Safe Java Implementation:
```java
public static long sumOfAP(long a, long d, long n) {
    return n * (2 * a + (n - 1) * d) / 2;
}
```

